{
  "name": "TestGoalFirstReturnsRecoveryValue",
  "comment": "Order=GoalFirst: when recovery's chain succeeds, handle.cs returns recoveryResult and sets Handled=true on the errored Call (lines 109-114). Pinned by the side-effect (%content% set inside recovery) AND by %!error% being null outside the scope — Handled=true and recoveryResult-return live in the same branch, so if a regression replaces them with Ok()+no-flag, %!error% would surface.",
  "step": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "throw error \"boom\", on error set %content% = \"from-recovery\", order GoalFirst",
      "line": {
        "number": 4
      },
